The attached image illustrates the in vivo kinetics of Nano-11 nanoparticles after intramuscular injection. Panel A shows whole-body fluorescence imaging of mice over 21 days, demonstrating that Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 is initially retained at the injection site and gradually cleared over time. Panel B, showing harvested internal organs at day 21, confirms that Nano-11 primarily remains at the injection site with minimal systemic distribution. Panel C quantitatively depicts the percentage of fluorescence intensity at the injection site over time, indicating a transient decrease by day 1, followed by a slight increase at day 2 (possibly due to edema resolving and less absorption of fluorescent signals), and then a sustained, gradual decrease, confirming Nano-11's retention and clearance from the injection site without widespread accumulation in other organs.